; The loudness a sonorant's frames take from the vowel next to it. First the LOUD card of AX's row of the phoneme
; table; then five cards a segment in: adjv (the vowel right after it in its word, 0 for none), prevv (the vowel
; before it, 0 for none), and the LOUD cards of the rows of adjv, prevv and nextv (the next vowel anywhere). Out two:
; for a voiced frame the loudness of adjv, else of prevv, else of AX; for the breathy first frame after P, T or K
; that of nextv.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03                    INP   lax      03-03: AX's loudness
  04            rec     INP   adjv     04-19: a segment
  05                    INP   prevv
  06                    INP   ladj
  07                    INP   lprev
  08                    INP   lnext
  09                    CLA   ladj
  10                    STO   lv
  11                    CLA   adjv
  12                    SUB   00
  13                    TAC   np
  14                    JMP   out
  15            np      CLA   lprev
  16                    STO   lv
  17                    CLA   prevv
  18                    SUB   00
  19                    TAC   ax
  20                    JMP   out
  21            ax      CLA   lax
  22                    STO   lv
  23            out     OUT   lv
  24                    OUT   lnext
  25                    JMP   rec
  30            lax     DATA  0
  31            adjv    DATA  0
  32            prevv   DATA  0
  33            ladj    DATA  0
  34            lprev   DATA  0
  35            lnext   DATA  0
  36            lv      DATA  0
